# The collector image GoReleaser publishes. It compiles nothing: the binary it
# copies is the one the CLI archives of the same release carry, already
# stamped, so the image and the archive cannot disagree about what they hold.
#
# NOT `FROM scratch`, which is what Dockerfile.agent uses. The agent speaks
# plain HTTP to one address on a veth and needs nothing else; the collector
# reaches stores and a Grafana that are ordinarily behind TLS, and a static
# binary with no CA bundle fails every one of them with `x509: certificate
# signed by unknown authority`. distroless/static carries the bundle and
# nothing executable beyond it — no shell, no package manager, so nothing to
# pin a version of and nothing to exploit with one.
#
# `nonroot` because the collector reads no local file it did not create and
# binds only what --prom is given; a container that needs no root should not
# have it.
#
# THIS IMAGE IS FOR `forward`. The deployment verbs (doctor, install, upgrade,
# uninstall) shell out to ssh and scp, which are not in here on purpose: a
# container that could reconfigure a router is a larger thing to hand someone
# than one that reads from it.
#
# TARGETPLATFORM is how GoReleaser's dockers_v2 lays the build context out: one
# directory per platform, each holding that platform's binary.
#
# There is no LABEL block here. GoReleaser passes the OCI labels on the build
# command line from .goreleaser.yaml, where the version, the commit and the
# date are known.
FROM gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot
ARG TARGETPLATFORM
COPY ${TARGETPLATFORM}/mikroscope /mikroscope
ENTRYPOINT ["/mikroscope"]
CMD ["forward"]
